(Bug #71: the refusal is not Print's alone. LANGUAGE.md:3226 promises a
 format specifier renders identically "whether the result is printed,
 written to a file, or built into a buffer", so a specifier the type cannot
 answer is refused in every sink - here a buffer `copy`, which used to
 accept it and silently drop the `:x`.)

a text called label is "hi".
a buffer called out is 64 bytes in size.
copy "{label:x}" to out.
Print "{out}".
